The registry-first sample tests/registry/rs.jsonl contains street names, house numbers and
coordinates from the Address Register (Адресни регистар) of the Republic Geodetic Authority of
Serbia (Републички геодетски завод, RGZ), house number export of 2025-06-10, made available
through the Open Data Portal of the Republic of Serbia under the Serbian Open Data Licence
(Лиценца за коришћење података - Портал отворених података Републике Србије,
https://data.gov.rs/sr/terms/).
Source: https://data.gov.rs/sr/datasets/adresni-registar/ (resource "Адресни регистар - кућни
бројеви (CSV)", https://download.geosrbija.rs/download-api/opendata-proxy/export?category=ar&layer=kucni_broj_ar&geometry=true&fileName=kucni_br_csv&format=csv).
That address is reachable only from Serbian networks; the copy used here is the export an
OpenAddresses contributor downloaded from it and posted
(https://github.com/openaddresses/openaddresses/issues/7199) at
https://bogdanupload.blob.core.windows.net/openaddresses/kucni_br_csv.zip, downloaded from there
on 2026-10-22.
Changes: coordinates were transformed from ETRS89 / UTM zone 34N (EPSG:25834) to EPSG:4326 with
DuckDB spatial / PROJ, a parenthesised qualifier was dropped from settlement and municipality
names ("БЕОГРАД (ЗЕМУН)" is written "БЕОГРАД"), and queries were constructed from registry fields.
Per-case prepared-CSV checksums and retrieval dates are recorded in the corpus;
docs/evaluation/registry/rs.md records the upstream checksums.
